Found one cotton series in the corpus: `archive/2024 cleanup/federal/cotton_output_working.csv` (4 observations, FY2010-11 → FY2013-14).

**Down — by 1.42 million bales, or about 11.7%.**

| Fiscal year | Million bales | YoY | Status |
|---|---|---|---|
| 2010-11 | 12.1523 | — | F |
| 2011-12 | 10.5049 | −13.6% | F |
| 2012-13 | 10.8365 | +3.2% | R |
| 2013-14 | 10.7295 | −1.0% | P |

Endpoint to endpoint: 12.1523 → 10.7295 = **−1.4228 million bales (−11.71%)**, a compound rate of about −4.1%/year.

The shape isn't a steady decline: essentially all of it is the single 2011-12 drop (−1.65m bales, −13.6%), followed by a partial recovery in 2012-13 and a flat 2013-14. Output never returns to the 2010-11 level within the window.

Two caveats on the endpoint:
- The 2013-14 figure is flagged **P (provisional)** and 2012-13 is **R (revised)**, so the −11.7% is sensitive to later revision. This is `vintage cotton_output::v0`, sourced from `economic_survey_2014`.
- The file is named `_working`, not a finalized series.

Also worth knowing: the same folder holds `Pakistan Economic Survey 2016-17 - perturbed values.pdf`, which likely carries a later vintage of this series (revised 2012-13/2013-14 plus later years). I couldn't read it — PDF text extraction isn't available in this session and the command to try it needed approval that a non-interactive session can't grant. If you want the revised numbers or a longer period, run it in an interactive session and I'll pull them.
